<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 3 September, from 590 to 1967.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">590</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gregory the Great is consecrated Pope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gregory, a former prefect of Rome turned monk, was consecrated pope after months of reluctance. He reorganised the Church's estates, sent missionaries to England and shaped the medieval papacy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1650</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cromwell routs the Scottish army at Dunbar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Trapped against the coast, Oliver Cromwell attacked at dawn and shattered David Leslie's larger Scottish army. Dunbar opened the way to the English conquest of Scotland.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1783</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Paris recognises American independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and American envoys signed the Treaty of Paris, ending the Revolutionary War and fixing the new nation's borders at the Mississippi. Britain signed separate treaties with France and Spain the same day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1939</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain and France declare war on Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">When Germany ignored ultimatums to withdraw from Poland, Britain and France declared war. Neville Chamberlain announced it to the nation in a sombre radio broadcast.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1943</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy secretly signs an armistice with the Allies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Italian and Allied officers signed the Armistice of Cassibile in Sicily, the same day British troops landed in Calabria. When it was announced on 8 September, Germany occupied much of Italy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1967</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sweden switches to driving on the right</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At 4.50 am all traffic in Sweden stopped, changed sides and restarted on the right. Dagen H, 'H Day', went remarkably smoothly after years of preparation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></li></ol>
